# oracle: pppm/dipole with point charges on SOME atoms only (id%4 == 1 gets +0.6, id%4 == 2 gets -0.6, the other 48 of 64 sc sites are neutral, net charge 0) and random dipoles on all sites (dipole/random 3317), pair lj/cut/dipole/long 3.5 1.0 (Coulomb cutoff below the nearest-neighbour distance, see w168pq_charge_dipole_auto), kspace_modify gewald 0.45 mesh 12 12 12 order 5, fix nve/sphere update dipole, 40 steps of 0.002: pe, evdwl, ecoul, elong, press and the per-atom forces, positions, dipoles and torques after the run
# oracle-files: w168pq_charge_partial_tq.dump
# measured with native LAMMPS (/home/roy/.local/bin/lmp, b332f28, installed DIPOLE and KSPACE packages): engine vs native fixture after 40 steps: max relative error 6.0e-15 (thermo), 6.7e-15 (per-atom forces, positions and velocities), 1.0e-15 (dipoles and torques); engine time 1.9 s (Node 24, loaded machine)
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 atomrel=1e-8 filerel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
units           lj
atom_style      hybrid sphere dipole
dimension       3
boundary        p p p
lattice         sc 0.30
region          box block 0 4 0 4 0 4
create_box      1 box
create_atoms    1 box
mass            1 1.0
set             group all diameter 1.0
set             group all density 1.0
variable        qi atom ((id%4==1)-(id%4==2))*0.6
set             group all charge v_qi
set             group all dipole/random 3317 1.0
pair_style      lj/cut/dipole/long 3.5 1.0
pair_coeff      1 1 1.0 1.0
kspace_style    pppm/dipole 1.0e-4
kspace_modify   gewald 0.45 mesh 12 12 12 order 5
neighbor        0.3 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check yes
velocity        all create 1.0 4928459 mom yes rot yes dist gaussian
fix             1 all nve/sphere update dipole
timestep        0.002
thermo          10
thermo_style    custom step pe evdwl ecoul elong press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g norm no
run             40
write_dump      all custom w168pq_charge_partial_tq.dump id mux muy muz tqx tqy tqz modify format float %.15g sort id
